    "body": "## Overview\n\nExternal prefix-cache-aware routers cannot determine a group's prefix reuse policy from its attention kind alone. This PR exposes `prefix_cacheable` and `prefix_replay_tokens` from the resolved spec through `EngineCore.get_kv_cache_group_metadata()`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Report whether each group participates in prefix caching and its required tail replay length.\n- Cover KpoolTail, Sliding MLA with bounded replay on/off, and uniform-type wrappers in the existing CPU metadata suite.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 \\\n  .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q \\\n  tests/v1/engine/test_kv_cache_group_metadata.py\n.venv/bin/ruff check vllm/v1/engine/core.py tests/v1/engine/test_kv_cache_group_metadata.py\n.venv/bin/ruff format --check vllm/v1/engine/core.py tests/v1/engine/test_kv_cache_group_metadata.py\ngit diff --check HEAD^ HEAD\n```\n\nResult: **5 passed**, including the existing DCP effective-block-size test. Omitting the added fields caused all 4 new cases to fail with `KeyError: 'prefix_cacheable'`. Ruff and whitespace checks passed.\n\nValidation ran in CPU mode with Python 3.12.3 and PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130. Model evaluation is not applicable to this metadata-only addition.\n\n## Details\n\nKpoolTail is classified as sliding-window attention but has `prefix_cacheable=False`. Bounded-replay Sliding MLA also opts out of shared prefix lookup and declares a replay window. These properties let external consumers identify participating groups and account for replay when estimating reuse benefits.\n\nRelated to [#48121](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/48121), which expands canonical metadata and frontend access. Its current diff does not include these two prefix-policy properties; this PR adds only those fields to the existing RPC.\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare the implementation and tests.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n\n</details>\n\n",
